{"base_rate":0.4540682414698163,"brier":0.15526640419947507,"bss":0.37364866329479773,"bss_hi":0.4540266427960816,"bss_lo":0.2941192396268171,"chart":{"base":[454.5,142.9],"fp":[364.0,275.3],"lead":"62,161.5 272,164.1 482,160.9 692,160.5","note":{"base":"skill 0.37 — higher than 72% of cities","fp":"low end +9pp, high end +8pp","lead":"day-1 error 2.0 °C — better than 6% of cities","rel":"promised 4% → rained 12%; promised 99% → rained 88%"},"rel":"84.5,416.3 297.2,283.8 564.8,155 683.4,87.7"},"country":"GG","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.07981627296587923,"ess":381.952031950819,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Saint Peter Port</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Saint Peter Port rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>88%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>9%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nGUERNSEY: AIRPORT, 5.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.37, ranked 60 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(33&ndash;106) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>226</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'><b>71%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>73%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>88%</b></td><td class='num'>161</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Saint Peter Port</b> <span class=\"muted\">Guernsey</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;45% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 45% of days.</p><p>The forecast did clearly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.37</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>33&ndash;106\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Saint Peter Port &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Saint Peter Port\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"61.77495575221239,372.3362831858407 96.30461538461539,316.6666666666667 147.82750000000001,255.61111111111111 230.84640000000002,163.6 310.067397260274,87.8082191780822 369.428051948052,36.909090909090935 407.1627329192546,18.0 407.1627329192546,29.30434782608694 369.428051948052,88.90909090909088 310.067397260274,162.6027397260274 230.84640000000002,241.25333333333333 147.82750000000001,321.3333333333333 96.30461538461539,363.3333333333333 61.77495575221239,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"216.71916010498688\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"216.71916010498688\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"61.77495575221239,349.78761061946904 96.30461538461539,312.0 147.82750000000001,255.61111111111111 230.84640000000002,202.42666666666665 310.067397260274,122.71232876712332 369.428051948052,117.27272727272725 407.1627329192546,63.217391304347814\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 226 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"61.77495575221239\" cy=\"349.78761061946904\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 11%&amp;#10;It rained 19% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"96.30461538461539\" cy=\"312.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 25%&amp;#10;It rained 35% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"147.82750000000001\" cy=\"255.61111111111111\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 49%&amp;#10;It rained 49% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"230.84640000000002\" cy=\"202.42666666666665\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 71%&amp;#10;It rained 71% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"310.067397260274\" cy=\"122.71232876712332\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 88%&amp;#10;It rained 73% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"369.428051948052\" cy=\"117.27272727272725\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 88% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 161 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"407.1627329192546\" cy=\"63.217391304347814\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(45%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Saint Peter Port the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.42) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.21).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>67%</td><td class='num'>0.208</td><td class='num'>14.8%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>0.243</td><td class='num'>10.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.319</td><td class='num'>7.2%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>56%</td><td class='num'>0.425</td><td class='num'>7.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":49.45981,"lon":-2.53527,"n":762,"n_cities":216,"name":"Saint Peter Port","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.010663716814159292,"n":226,"obs":0.08849557522123894,"sig":true},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.10820512820512822,"n":78,"obs":0.19230769230769232,"sig":true},{"hi":0.38,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.25375000000000003,"n":72,"obs":0.3472222222222222,"sig":false},{"hi":0.63,"lo":0.38,"mean":0.48826666666666674,"n":75,"obs":0.49333333333333335,"sig":false},{"hi":0.83,"lo":0.63,"mean":0.712054794520548,"n":73,"obs":0.7123287671232876,"sig":false},{"hi":0.95,"lo":0.83,"mean":0.8797402597402598,"n":77,"obs":0.7272727272727273,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.95,"mean":0.9863354037267079,"n":161,"obs":0.8757763975155279,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.5,"provisional":false,"rank":60,"rank_hi":106.0,"rank_lo":33.0,"reliability":0.008280437296538226,"resolution":0.09938798542880017,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"saint-peter-port","station":"GUERNSEY: AIRPORT","timezone":"Europe/Guernsey"}